400
00:43:57,260 --> 00:44:10,179
Summarizing a text or distilling its essential concepts into a paragraph or two is a useful study tool as well as good writing practice.

401
00:44:10,179 --> 00:44:20,320
And a summary has two aims. One to reproduce the overarching ideas in a text identifying the general concepts that run through the entire piece.

402
00:44:20,500 --> 00:44:27,639
And second to express these overarching ideas using a precise specific language.

403
00:44:27,639 --> 00:44:38,820
When you summarize, you cannot rely on the language the author has used to develop his or her points.

404
00:44:38,920 --> 00:44:46,260
And you must find a way to give an overview of these points without your own sentences becoming too general.

405
00:44:46,260 --> 00:44:59,019
You must also make decisions about which concepts to live in and which to omit, taking into consideration your purposes in summarizing and also your view of what is important in this text.

406
00:44:59,420 --> 00:45:05,960
When you summarize, you highlight the key points, the important points, the important information.

407
00:45:05,960 --> 00:45:12,740
And then you write this information using your own words.

408
00:45:12,740 --> 00:45:15,760
You don't change the meaning. You use your own words.

409
00:45:15,920 --> 00:45:20,059
So that means you use different structure and different words.

410
00:45:20,260 --> 00:45:23,059
But you shouldn't change the meaning.

411
00:45:23,720 --> 00:45:58,740
You just mention the important points in the text.

